## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end production-readiness: real-time latency, privacy across tenants, and governance with canary rollouts and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time inference with Vertex AI online endpoints and low-latency feature streaming
- Per-tenant feature stores for isolation; centralized ensemble for shared knowledge
- Privacy preservation via secure aggregation or differential privacy for cross-tenant signals
- Data provenance in BigQuery, Dataflow preprocessing, and strict cost controls with budgets
- Canary rollout, rollback criteria, and automated retraining cadence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: secure aggregation wrapper (conceptual)
function aggregateSecurely(tenantSignals) {
  // apply per-tenant masking, sum-aggregation, and reveal only aggregated result
  // actual DP/secure-aggregation libs would be used in prod
  const masked = tenantSignals.map(s => s + randomMask());
  return masked.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) - totalMask(masked.length);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift and decide retraining triggers for the ensemble model?
- What strategies ensure cost control without hurting latency or accuracy?

## Why This Is Asked
Designing adaptive models under load tests real-time orchestration and governance in GCP. It probes latency budgeting, feature-store usage, and rollback mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-model online/offline design
- Vertex AI Endpoints traffic splitting
- Real-time feature engineering with Pub/Sub/Dataflow/Feature Store
- Drift and latency monitoring, rollback via registry pinning
- Data Catalog lineage for auditability

## Code Example
```javascript
function chooseModel(latency, budget){
  if (latency <= 100 && budget > 0){
    return 'lightweight';
  }
  return 'heavy';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a modular, governance-minded pipeline that handles multilingual data and targeted evaluation without overcomplication. It emphasizes per-language data management, explainability, and rollback—common beginner-friendly MLOps concerns.

## Key Concepts
- Language-based routing and partitioning
- Per-language training subsets in Vertex AI
- Unified endpoint with traffic-splitting by language
- Explainable AI per language
- Drift monitoring and simple rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-configuration sketch for per-language training
const trainingPlan = {
